msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6670
msgid "v0.3.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6674
msgid ""
"`and`, `or`, `&&`, `||` have been added as subprocess logical operators, by "
"popular demand!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6676
msgid ""
"Subprocesses may be negated with `not` and grouped together with parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6678
msgid "New framework for writing xonsh extensions, called `xontribs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6679
msgid ""
"Added a new shell type `'none'`, used to avoid importing `readline` or "
"`prompt_toolkit` when running scripts or running a single command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6682
msgid "New: [sudo]{.title-ref} functionality on Windows through an alias"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6683
msgid ""
"Automatically enhance colors for readability in the default terminal (cmd."
"exe) on Windows. This functionality can be enabled/disabled with the \\"
"$INTENSIFY_COLORS_ON_WIN environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6686
msgid ""
"Added `Ellipsis` lookup to `__xonsh_env__` to allow environment variable "
"checks, e.g. `'HOME' in ${...}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6688
msgid ""
"Added an option to update `os.environ` every time the xonsh environment "
"changes. This is disabled by default but can be enabled by setting "
"`$UPDATE_OS_ENVIRON` to True."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6691
msgid ""
"Added Windows \\'cmd.exe\\' as a foreign shell. This gives xonsh the ability "
"to source Windows Batch files (.bat and .cmd). Calling `source-cmd script."
"bat` or the alias `source-bat script.bat` will call the bat file and changes "
"to the environment variables will be reflected in xonsh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6696
msgid ""
"Added an alias for the conda environment activate/deactivate batch scripts "
"when running the Anaconda python distribution on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6698
msgid ""
"Added a menu entry to launch xonsh when installing xonsh from a conda package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6700
msgid ""
"Added a new `which` alias that supports both regular `which` and also "
"searches through xonsh aliases. A pure python implementation of `which` is "
"used. Thanks to Trent Mick. <https://github.com/trentm/which/>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6704
msgid "Added support for prompt toolkit v1.0.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6705
msgid ""
"Added `$XONSH_CACHE_SCRIPTS` and `$XONSH_CACHE_EVERYTHING` environment "
"variables to control caching of scripts and interactive commands. These can "
"also be controlled by command line options `--no-script-cache` and `--cache-"
"everything` when starting xonsh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6709
msgid ""
"Added a workaround to allow ctrl-c to interrupt reverse incremental search "
"in the readline shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6714
msgid ""
"Running scripts through xonsh (or running a single command with `-c`) no "
"longer runs the user\\'s rc file, unless the `--login` option is specified. "
"Also avoids loading aliases and environments from foreign shells, as well as "
"loading bash completions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6718
msgid ""
"rc files are now compiled and cached, to avoid re-parsing when they "
"haven\\'t changed. Scripts are also compiled and cached, and there is the "
"option to cache interactive commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6721
msgid ""
"Left and Right arrows in the `prompt_toolkit` shell now wrap in multiline "
"environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6723
msgid ""
"Regexpath matching with backticks, now returns an empty list in python mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6725
msgid "Pygments added as a dependency for the conda package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6726
msgid ""
"Foreign shells now allow for setting exit-on-error commands before and after "
"all other commands via the `seterrprevcmd` and `seterrpostcmd` arguments. "
"Sensinble defaults are provided for existing shells."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6730
msgid ""
"PLY is no longer a external dependency but is bundled in xonsh/ply. Xonsh "
"can therefore run without any external dependencies, although having prompt-"
"toolkit recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6733
msgid ""
"Provide better user feedback when running `which` in a platform that "
"doesn\\'t provide it (e.g. Windows)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6735
msgid ""
"The lexer now uses a custom tokenizer that handles regex globs in the proper "
"way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6740
msgid "Fixed bug with loading prompt-toolkit shell \\< v0.57."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6741
msgid ""
"Fixed bug with prompt-toolkit completion when the cursor is not at the end "
"of the line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6743
msgid ""
"Aliases will now evaluate environment variables and other expansions at "
"execution time rather than passing through a literal string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6745
msgid ""
"Fixed environment variables from os.environ not being loaded when a running "
"a script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6747
msgid "The readline shell will now load the inputrc files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6748
msgid "Fixed bug that prevented [source-alias]{.title-ref} from working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6749
msgid "Now able to `^C` the xonfig wizard on start up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6750
msgid ""
"Fixed deadlock on Windows when running subprocess that generates enough "
"output to fill the OS pipe buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6752
msgid ""
"Sourcing foreign shells will now return a non-zero exit code if the source "
"operation failed for some reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6754
msgid ""
"Fixed PermissionError when running commands in directories without read "
"permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6756
msgid ""
"Prevent Windows fixups from overriding environment vars in static config"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6758
msgid ""
"Fixed Optional Github project status to reflect added/removed files via "
"git_dirty_working_directory()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6760
msgid ""
"Fixed xonsh.exe launcher on Windows, when Python install directory has a "
"space in it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6762
msgid ""
"Fixed [\\$CDPATH]{.title-ref} to support [\\~]{.title-ref} and environments "
"variables in its items"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6765
msgid "v0.2.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6769
msgid ""
"Added new valid `$SHELL_TYPE` called `'best'`. This selects the best value "
"for the concrete shell type based on the availability on the user\\'s "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6772
msgid ""
"New environment variable `$XONSH_COLOR_STYLE` will set the color mapping for "
"all of xonsh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6774
msgid ""
"New `XonshStyle` pygments style will determine the appropriate color mapping "
"based on `$XONSH_COLOR_STYLE`. The associated `xonsh_style_proxy()` is "
"intended for wrapping `XonshStyle` when actually being used by pygments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6778
msgid ""
"The functions `print_color()` and `format_color()` found in `xonsh.tools` "
"dispatch to the approriate shell color handling and may be used from "
"anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6781
msgid ""
"`xonsh.tools.HAVE_PYGMENTS` flag now denotes if pygments is installed and "
"available on the users system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6783
msgid ""
"The `ansi_colors` module is now available for handling ANSI color codes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6785
msgid "`?` and `??` operator output now has colored titles, like in IPython."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6787
msgid "`??` will syntax highlight source code if pygments is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6788
msgid "Python mode output is now syntax highlighted if pygments is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6790
msgid ""
"New `$RIGHT_PROMPT` environment variable for displaying right-aligned text "
"in prompt-toolkit shell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6792
msgid ""
"Added `!(...)` operator, which returns an object representing the result of "
"running a command. The truth value of this object is True if the return code "
"is equal to zero and False otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6795
msgid ""
"Optional dependency on the win_unicode_console package to enable unicode "
"support in cmd.exe on Windows. This can be disabled/enabled with the "
"`$WIN_UNICODE_CONSOLE` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6801
msgid "Updated `$SHELL_TYPE` default to `'best'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6802
msgid ""
"Shell classes are now responsible for implementing their own color "
"formatting and printing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6804
msgid ""
"Prompt coloring, history diffing, and tracing uses new color handling "
"capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6806
msgid ""
"New `Token.Color` token for xonsh color names, e.g. we now use `Token.Color."
"RED` rather than `Token.RED`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6808
msgid ""
"Untracked files in git are ignored when determining if a git workdir is is "
"dirty. This affects the coloring of the branch label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../changelog.md:6810
msgid ""
"Regular expression globbing now uses `re.fullmatch` instead of `re.match`, "
"and the result of an empty regex glob does not cause the argument to be "
"deleted."
msgstr ""

